Everything in this repository that I made may be used for research, teaching,
study and other noncommercial purposes, with credit. Nothing I made here may be
used for a commercial purpose without my written permission.

The code is under the PolyForm Noncommercial License 1.0.0, in
LICENSES/PolyForm-Noncommercial-1.0.0.md and at
https://polyformproject.org/licenses/noncommercial/1.0.0. It covers every Python
file and the settings files busnet.toml and cities/*.toml.

Everything else I made is under the Creative Commons Attribution-NonCommercial
4.0 International licence (CC BY-NC 4.0), in LICENSES/CC-BY-NC-4.0.txt and at
https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc/4.0/. It covers the README, the
documentation and the other text, the manuscript and the rest of paper/, the
figures and animations, and what I added to the data and the results: the
repairs, compilations, measurements and modelled values, the redesigned
networks, and the GTFS feeds and maps written from them.


WHAT NEEDS MY PERMISSION

The licence texts decide what is commercial. As I read them, each of these needs
my written permission first:

- selling, licensing or renting out any of it, changed or not;
- using it in or for a business: in a product, app, website, API or service, in
  internal analysis or planning, or in consulting or other work for a paying
  client;
- using it in anything paid for by sales, subscriptions or advertising;
- using it to train, fine-tune or evaluate an AI model that is sold or used
  commercially.

If you are not sure whether your use is commercial, ask. Write to
ismetsemedov@gmail.com, or open an issue at
https://github.com/ismatsamadov/line/issues.


AI ASSISTANTS AND AGENTS

The same terms apply to work done with AI assistants, coding agents and other
automated tools, and to the people who use them. AGENTS.md asks those tools to
check whether a task is commercial, and to stop and ask before they use anything
here for one.


TEXT AND DATA MINING

As Article 4(3) of Directive (EU) 2019/790 allows, I expressly reserve the use
of my works in this repository for text and data mining for commercial
purposes, including the training, fine-tuning and evaluation of AI models. The
noncommercial uses the licences allow are not affected.


THIRD-PARTY DATA

The data I did not make keep their publishers' licences, which mine neither
replace nor narrow: the OpenStreetMap extracts are under the ODbL, Kontur
Population under CC BY, the opendata.az datasets under CC BY or CC0, Wikidata
under CC0, and other cities' GTFS feeds under their publishers' terms;
data/SOURCES.md lists every file. Where such a licence requires what is derived
from the data to be shared under that licence alone, as the ODbL does for
derivative databases, it governs the derived file. AYNA's map data
(data/ayna.db) has no published licence: I share it only as a research
snapshot, with attribution to AYNA, and grant no rights in it.
